WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.495
Know the processes connecting igneous, sedimentary, and metamorphic rock. Weathering breaks

00:00:05.495 --> 00:00:10.641
rock down. Erosion and transport move the pieces; deposition drops them.

00:00:11.475 --> 00:00:16.489
Burial packs sediment together. Compaction and cementation turn loose grains into

00:00:16.489 --> 00:00:17.400
sedimentary rock.

00:00:19.475 --> 00:00:24.060
Heat and pressure change solid rock into metamorphic rock. Metamorphism does

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.311
not require melting.

00:00:27.475 --> 00:00:31.728
Melting makes magma; cooling makes igneous rock. His key point: the

00:00:31.728 --> 00:00:35.595
rock cycle has many possible routes, not one fixed loop.
